//! Read chart parts from an [`XmlTree`] (Tier 1J): `c:chartSpace`, `cx:chartSpace`, a chart's
//! drawing, and its style and colour parts.
//!
//! One reader per schema type, generated by `tools/chart-codegen/generate.py` into `chart/`.
//! By the same rule as the rest of this crate: a usable value goes in the model, an unusable
//! one is reported and left out, and everything stays in the tree. Unlike a slide part, a
//! chart that cannot be read refuses nothing: it is set aside and reported, and the deck
//! opens and saves with its bytes (owner instruction 24).
//!
//! **An embedded workbook is never opened (`SEC-P09`).** A chart's cached values are what the
//! model holds. The `package` relationship is recorded by name, and no byte of its target is
//! read, so a hostile workbook cannot reach this code.
//!
//! Evidence: the vendored schemas. `T1J-04`'s signed axis id is from `poi-bar-chart-mac` and
//! `pypptx-chart-type-mac`, both Mac PowerPoint by their own `app.xml`.

